.TH SDL_TryLockRWLockForReading 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_TryLockRWLockForReading \- Try to lock a read/write lock _for reading_ without blocking.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_mutex.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_TryLockRWLockForReading(SDL_RWLock *rwlock);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This works just like
.BR SDL_LockRWLockForReading (),
but if the rwlock is not available, then this function returns false immediately\[char46]
.PP
This technique is useful if you need access to a resource but don\(aqt want to wait for it, and will return to it to try again later\[char46]
.PP
Trying to lock for read-only access can succeed if other threads are holding read-only locks, as this won\(aqt prevent access\[char46]
.PP
This function returns true if passed a NULL rwlock\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I rwlock
the rwlock to try to lock\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success, false if the lock would block\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_LockRWLockForReading (3),
.BR SDL_TryLockRWLockForWriting (3),
.BR SDL_UnlockRWLock (3)
